                <pb facs="0265" n="231" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 185.</note>
                <head>Mr. Fish to Baron Gerolt.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 22, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, Secretary of State of the United States, has the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of the communication addressed to him on the 15th
                    instant by Baron Gerolt, the envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of
                    the North German Union, relating to the complaints made by the governments of
                    North Germany and France as to alleged violations of international law in their
                    respective military operations.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself of this opportunity to renew to Baron Gerolt the
                    assurance of his highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
